board.ps1`\n"},"partialJson":"{\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\吗喽\\\\.openclaw\\\\workspace\\\\skills\\\\edict-dashboard-autostart\\\\SKILL.md\",\"content\":\"---\\nname: edict-dashboard-autostart\\ndescription: Auto-start and verify the 三省六部 (Edict) web dashboard when the user asks to start/launch/open 三省六部, 军机处看板, Edict dashboard, or asks “网页看板在哪”. Use this skill to bring up the dashboard service at http://127.0.0.1:7891 and return the access URL quickly.\\n---\\n\\n# Edict Dashboard Autostart\\n\\n1. Detect trigger intent.\\n   - Trigger on requests like: “三省六部启动”, “启动看板”, “打开军机处”, “Edict dashboard”, “网页看板在哪”.\\n\\n2. Ensure service is reachable on `127.0.0.1:7891`.\\n   - First check whether port 7891 is already listening.\\n   - If listening, do not start a duplicate process.\\n\\n3. If not running, start dashboard backend.\\n   - Working directory: `C:\\\\Users\\\\吗喽\\\\.openclaw\\\\workspace\\\\edict`\\n   - Start command: `python dashboard/server.py`\\n   - Use background execution so chat is not blocked.\\n\\n4. Verify startup.\\n   - Wait briefly, then confirm the process is alive or port is listening.\\n   - If startup fails, report the error and suggest checking Python/environment.\\n\\n5. Reply format.\\n   - Keep it short and action-first.\\n   - Include direct URL: `http://127.0.0.1:7891`\\n   - If LAN is needed, also include `http://<local-ip>:7891` when available.\\n\\n## Script\\n\\nUse `scripts/start-edict-dashboard.ps1` for deterministic startup/check operations.\\n\\n- Check only:\\n  - `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/start-edict-dashboard.ps1 -CheckOnly`\\n- Start if needed:\\n  - `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/start-edict-dashboard.ps1`\\n\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.3-codex","usage":{"input":1047,"output":626,"cacheRead":35840,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":37513,"cost":{"input":0.00183225,"output":0.008764,"cacheRead":0.006272,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01686825}},"