\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\concepts\\memory.md:35: - `memory_search` �� semantic recall over indexed snippets.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\concepts\\memory.md:46: - Decisions, preferences, and durable facts go to `MEMORY.md`.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\concepts\\memory.md:94: OpenClaw can build a small vector index over `MEMORY.md` and `memory/*.md` so\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\concepts\\memory.md:158:   timers are armed even before the first `memory_search` call.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\concepts\\memory.md:198:   `memory_search` (`search`, `vsearch`, `query`).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\concepts\\memory.md:199: - `includeDefaultMemory` (default `true`): auto-index `MEMORY.md` + `memory/**/*.md`.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\concepts\\memory.md:221:   `qmd/<collection>/<relative-path>` in `memory_search` results; `memory_get`\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\concepts\\memory.md:225:   `~/.openclaw/agents/<id>/qmd/sessions/`, so `memory_search` can recall recent\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\concepts\\memory.md:227: - `memory_search` snippets now include a `Source: <path#line>` footer when\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\concepts\\memory.md:377: - `memory_search` �� returns snippets with file + line ranges.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\concepts\\memory.md:388: - `memory_search` semantically searches Markdown chunks (~400 token target, 80-token overlap) from `MEMORY.md` + `memory/**/*.md`. It returns snippet text (capped ~700 chars), file path, line range, score, provider/model, and whether we fell back from local �� remote embeddings. No full file payload is returned.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\concepts\\memory.md:389: - `memory_get` reads a specific memory Markdown file (workspace-relative), optionally from a starting line and for N lines. Paths outside `MEMORY.md` / `memory/` are rejected.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\concepts\\memory.md:394: - File type: Markdown only (`MEMORY.md`, `memory/**/*.md`).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\concepts\\memory.md:396: - Freshness: watcher on `MEMORY.md` + `memory/` marks the index dirty (debounce 1.5s). Sync is scheduled on session start, on search, or on an interval and runs asynchronously. Session transcripts use delta thresholds to trigger background sync.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\concepts\\memory.md:513: **When to enable:** If you notice `memory_search` returning redundant or near-duplicate snippets,\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\concepts\\memory.md:540: - `MEMORY.md` (root memory file)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\concepts\\memory.md:637: You can optionally index **session transcripts** and surface them via `memory_search`.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\concepts\\memory.md:655: - `memory_search` never blocks on indexing; results can be slightly stale until background sync finishes.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\concepts\\system-prompt.md:62: - `MEMORY.md` and/or `memory.md` (when present in the workspace; either or both may be injected)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\concepts\\system-prompt.md:65: means they consume tokens. Keep them concise �� especially `MEMORY.md`, which can\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\doc