g\":\"en\",\"tgt_lang\":\"zh-CN\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-02-01T13:36:36Z\"}\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\.i18n\\zh-CN.tm.jsonl:649: {\"cache_key\":\"7ea531b1b4d75bfda8cb0a3a62e895b86310ab3f79a08cdcaddc1f2ccc61fbc2\",\"segment_id\":\"index.md:3f8466cd9cb153d0\",\"source_path\":\"index.md\",\"text_hash\":\"3f8466cd9cb153d0c78a88f6a209e2206992db28c6dab45424132dc187974e2b\",\"text\":\"Note: legacy Claude/Codex/Gemini/Opencode paths have been removed; Pi is the only coding-agent path.\",\"translated\":\"ע�⣺�ɰ� Claude/Codex/Gemini/Opencode ·�����Ƴ���Pi ��Ψһ�ı��������·����\",\"provider\":\"pi\",\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-5\",\"src_lang\":\"en\",\"tgt_lang\":\"zh-CN\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-02-01T13:31:04Z\"}\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\.i18n\\zh-CN.tm.jsonl:1316: {\"cache_key\":\"fe28d810ff498a350b586785445582bed45cf1b1de02ea8be1569cf0da546ecc\",\"segment_id\":\"index.md:3f8466cd9cb153d0\",\"source_path\":\"index.md\",\"text_hash\":\"3f8466cd9cb153d0c78a88f6a209e2206992db28c6dab45424132dc187974e2b\",\"text\":\"Note: legacy Claude/Codex/Gemini/Opencode paths have been removed; Pi is the only coding-agent path.\",\"translated\":\"ע�⣺�ɰ� Claude/Codex/Gemini/Opencode ·���ѱ��Ƴ���Pi ��Ψһ�ı�� ������ ·����\",\"provider\":\"pi\",\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-5\",\"src_lang\":\"en\",\"tgt_lang\":\"zh-CN\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-02-01T12:51:20Z\"}\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\cron-jobs.md:31: - Legacy fallback remains for stored jobs with `notify: true` when `cron.webhook` is set, migrate those jobs to webhook delivery mode.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\cron-jobs.md:109: In agent tool calls, `jobId` is canonical; legacy `id` is accepted for compatibility.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\cron-jobs.md:220: - Deprecated fallback: stored legacy jobs with `notify: true` still post to `cron.webhook` (if configured), with a warning so you can migrate to `delivery.mode = \"webhook\"`.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\cron-jobs.md:413:     webhook: \"https://example.invalid/legacy\", // deprecated fallback for stored notify:true jobs\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\cron-jobs.md:437: - Deprecated fallback: stored legacy jobs with `notify: true` still use `cron.webhook` when present.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\hooks.md:497: ### Legacy Config Format (Still Supported)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\hooks.md:520: **Migration**: Use the new discovery-based system for new hooks. Legacy handlers are loaded after directory-based hooks.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\hooks.md:971: ### From Legacy Config to Discovery\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\webhook.md:119: Compatibility config (legacy behavior):\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:12: Status: bundled plugin that talks to the BlueBubbles macOS server over HTTP. **Recommended for iMessage integration** due to its richer API and easier setup compared to the legacy imsg channel.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:372:     `channels.discord.dmPolicy` controls DM access (legacy: `channels.discord.dm.policy`):\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:376:     - `open` (requires `channels.discord.allowFrom` to include `\"*\"`; legacy: `channels.discord.dm.allowFrom`)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:579:     - `channels.discord.streamMode` is a legacy alias and is auto-migrated.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:983: OpenClaw uses Discord components v2 for exec approvals and cross-context markers. Discord message actions can also accept `components` for custom UI (advanced; requires Carbon component instances), while legacy `embeds` remain available but are not recommended.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:1161:     - DM policy disabled: `channels.discord.dmPolicy=\"disabled\"` (legacy: `channels.discord.dm.policy`)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:1202: - streaming: `streaming` (legacy alias: `streamMode`), `draftChunk`, `blockStreaming`, `blockStreamingCoalesce`\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\feishu.md:24: openclaw plugins install @openclaw/feishu\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\googlechat.md:232:    openclaw plugins list | grep googlechat\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\groups.md:261:   Legacy unprefixed keys are still accepted and matched as `id:` only.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\imessage.md:2: summary: \"Legacy iMessage support via imsg (JSON-RPC over stdio). New setups should use BlueBubbles.\"\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\imessage.md:9: # iMessage (legacy: imsg)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\imessage.md:14: The `imsg` integration is legacy and may be removed in a future release.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\imessage.md:17: Status: legacy external CLI integration. Gateway spawns `imsg rpc` and communicates over JSON-RPC on stdio (no separate daemon/port).\r\nC:\