t entries from pairing-store files in allowlist migration flows.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\telegram.md:846: - `channels.telegram.groupAllowFrom`: group sender allowlist (numeric Telegram user IDs). `openclaw doctor --fix` can resolve legacy `@username` entries to IDs. Non-numeric entries are ignored at auth time. Group auth does not use DM pairing-store fallback (`2026.2.25+`).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\telegram.md:873: - `channels.telegram.streaming`: `off | partial | block | progress` (live stream preview; default: `partial`; `progress` maps to `partial`; `block` is legacy preview mode compatibility). Telegram preview streaming uses a single preview message that is edited in place.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\tlon.md:24: openclaw plugins install @openclaw/tlon\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\tlon.md:30: openclaw plugins install ./extensions/tlon\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\twitch.md:19: openclaw plugins install @openclaw/twitch\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\twitch.md:25: openclaw plugins install ./extensions/twitch\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\whatsapp.md:341: - WhatsApp uses `channels.whatsapp.ackReaction` (legacy `messages.ackReaction` is not used here)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\whatsapp.md:352:   <Accordion title=\"Credential paths and legacy compatibility\">\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\whatsapp.md:355:     - legacy default auth in `~/.openclaw/credentials/` is still recognized/migrated for default-account flows\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\whatsapp.md:361:     In legacy auth directories, `oauth.json` is preserved while Baileys auth files are removed.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\zalo.md:16: - Install via CLI: `openclaw plugins install @openclaw/zalo`\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\zalo.md:23:    - From a source checkout: `openclaw plugins install ./extensions/zalo`\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\zalo.md:24:    - From npm (if published): `openclaw plugins install @openclaw/zalo`\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\zalouser.md:19: - Install via CLI: `openclaw plugins install @openclaw/zalouser`\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\zalouser.md:20: - Or from a source checkout: `openclaw plugins install ./extensions/zalouser`\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\cli\\clawbot.md:2: summary: \"CLI reference for `openclaw clawbot` (legacy alias namespace)\"\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\cli\\clawbot.md:11: Legacy alias namespace kept for backwards compatibility.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\cli\\config.md:46: Use `--strict-json` to require JSON5 parsing. `--json` remains supported as a legacy alias.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\cli\\daemon.md:2: summary: \"CLI reference for `openclaw daemon` (legacy alias for gateway service management)\"\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\cli\\daemon.md:11: Legacy alias for Gateway service management commands.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\cli\\index.md:58: - [`daemon`](/cli/daemon) (legacy alias for gateway service commands)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\opencla